<article class="env-corollary" id="0684">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0684">Corollary <span data-tag="0684">9.3.2.22</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be a small uncountable regular cardinal. Then the inclusion functor $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \kappa } \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ as an $\operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }$-completion of $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \kappa }$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Variant <a data-tag="06FU" href="/tag/06FU">9.3.2.21</a> in the special case where $\lambda =  \Omega $ is a strongly inaccessible cardinal (here the inequality $\kappa &lt; \lambda $ guarantees that $\kappa \triangleleft \lambda $; see Example <a data-tag="061R" href="/tag/061R">9.1.7.11</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
